project/editor-docked-panel-chrome: spoint's editor (client/editor/*) must use the DOCKED panel variant from anentrypoint-design editor-primitives.css, NOT the dashboard .panel/.panel-inline card (rounded var(--r-3), margin var(--space-5), box-shadow, oversized panel-head padding) which renders floating cards over the viewport and reads as jank. Kit classes (published 0.0.182+, consumed via unpkg @latest): .ds-ep-panel (flush, square, no margin/shadow, full-height flex column, overflow hidden) + .ds-ep-panel-head (6px/10px dense bordered) + .ds-ep-panel-body(.flush) + .ds-ep-panel-section (collapses display:none when :empty so empty app-prop mounts show no stray dashed rule) + .ds-ep-statusbar (26px dense strip, buttons forced to 20px). CRITICAL kit fix: .ds-ep-tabs-body was display:block which collapsed a full-height docked child to h:0 -> now display:flex flex-direction:column. EditorInspector.createEditorInspector never called render() on construction -> the 'Select an entity' empty-state never painted before a selection; added an initial render() call; EmptyState takes {text} not {title}. SceneHierarchy TreeItem tag must be suppressed when it equals the label or root entities render 'name name'. EditorShell status uses a custom .ds-ep-statusbar div, not the tall 68px C.Status. Witnessed live editor-published.png against published 0.0.182: 3-column docked layout, flush square full-height, status 26px, empty-state centered.